<%- include('partials/head') %>
<%
  const yes = '<svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-ok"></use></svg><span class="sr-only">Included</span>';
  const no = '<span class="no">No</span>';
%>

<div class="doc">
  <header class="page-head">
    <h1>Pricing</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Screening is free forever. Protection Suite is <%= price.symbol %><%= price.amount %> a month
      per server<% if (plans.includes('yearly')) { %>, <%= price.symbol %><%= prices.yearly %> a year<% } %><%
        if (plans.includes('lifetime')) { %>, or <%= price.symbol %><%= prices.lifetime %> once<% } %><%
        if (trial.offered) { %>, with the first <%= trial.days %> days free on monthly and yearly<% } %>.
      One licence covers both BotApprove and RaidProtector in that server.
    </p>
  </header>

  <% if (!plans.length) { %>
    <div class="notice warn">
      <strong>Card payment is not open yet</strong>
      <p>
        Checkout is switched off while the payment account is being set up, so nothing on this page
        can be bought right now. Everything free stays free and is working normally: the approval
        gate, keyword blocking, the audit trail and tamper detection do not depend on any of this.
      </p>
      <p>
        When card payment opens, every server owner running BotApprove is told directly, once.
        Holding a licence key already? It works now and will keep working.
      </p>
    </div>
  <% } %>

  <div class="plans">
    <section class="plan" aria-labelledby="plan-free">
      <p class="form-label">Plan</p>
      <h2 id="plan-free">Free</h2>
      <p><span class="plan-free-price"><%= price.symbol %>0</span></p>
      <p>
        No card, no trial, no expiry. This is the whole approval gate<% if (repoUrl) { %>, and it is
        <a href="<%= repoUrl %>" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">open source</a><% } %>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="plan suite" aria-labelledby="plan-suite">
      <p class="form-label">Licence, one server</p>
      <h2 id="plan-suite">Protection Suite</h2>
      <ul class="covers" aria-label="Covers">
        <li><span class="prod-mark ba"><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#m-ba"></use></svg></span>BotApprove</li>
        <li><span class="prod-mark rp"><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#m-rp"></use></svg></span>RaidProtector <span class="badge">Beta</span></li>
      </ul>
      <ul class="options">
        <li>
          <div>
            <span class="amount"><%= price.symbol %><%= price.amount %></span>
            <span class="per">a month, per server</span>
          </div>
          <% if (plans.includes('monthly')) { %>
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/subscribe?plan=monthly">Get monthly, <%= price.symbol %><%= price.amount %></a>
          <% } %>
        </li>
        <% if (plans.includes('yearly')) { %>
          <li>
            <div>
              <span class="amount"><%= price.symbol %><%= prices.yearly %></span>
              <span class="per">a year, two months free</span>
            </div>
            <a class="btn" href="/subscribe?plan=yearly">Get yearly, <%= price.symbol %><%= prices.yearly %></a>
          </li>
        <% } %>
        <% if (plans.includes('lifetime')) { %>
          <li>
            <div>
              <span class="amount"><%= price.symbol %><%= prices.lifetime %></span>
              <span class="per">
                once, for as long as BotApprove operates<%
                  if (lifetime.capped) { %>. <%= lifetime.remaining %> of <%= lifetime.cap %> left<% } %>.
              </span>
            </div>
            <a class="btn" href="/subscribe?plan=lifetime">Get lifetime, <%= price.symbol %><%= prices.lifetime %></a>
          </li>
        <% } else if (lifetime.soldOut) { %>
          <li>
            <div>
              <span class="amount faint"><%= price.symbol %><%= prices.lifetime %></span>
              <span class="per">
                once, <strong>sold out</strong>. Email
                <a href="mailto:<%= contactEmail %>"><%= contactEmail %></a> if you need one.
              </span>
            </div>
          </li>
        <% } %>
      </ul>
      <% if (trial.offered) { %>
        <p>
          <strong><%= trial.days %> days free</strong> on the monthly and yearly plans, then billing
          starts. Cancel during the trial and you are not charged. One trial per server.
        </p>
      <% } %>
      <% if (plans.length) { %><p>You pick which server it applies to next.</p><% } %>
    </section>
  </div>

  <p class="hint">
    Priced per server, not per member, so a large community costs the same as a small one.
    Holding a licence key instead? Redeem it on your server's Licence tab and pay nothing.
  </p>

  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="compare-title">
    <div class="band-head">
      <h2 id="compare-title">What each plan includes</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Nothing that protects a server is ever behind the paywall. Premium is extras, and the
        dashboard says which is which.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="compare">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Feature</th>
            <th scope="col" class="col-mark">Free</th>
            <th scope="col" class="col-mark">Suite</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="group"><th scope="colgroup" colspan="3">BotApprove</th></tr>
          <% freeFeatures.forEach((f) => { %>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row"><%= f.name %><span class="blurb"><%= f.blurb %></span></th>
              <td class="col-mark"><%- yes %></td>
              <td class="col-mark"><%- yes %></td>
            </tr>
          <% }) %>
          <% premiumFeatures.forEach((f) => { %>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row"><%= f.name %><span class="blurb"><%= f.blurb %></span></th>
              <td class="col-mark"><%- no %></td>
              <td class="col-mark"><%- yes %></td>
            </tr>
          <% }) %>
          <tr class="group"><th scope="colgroup" colspan="3">RaidProtector</th></tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">RaidProtector, while the beta runs<span class="blurb">Raid detection, a response you can undo, and a record of every incident.</span></th>
            <td class="col-mark"><%- no %></td>
            <td class="col-mark"><%- yes %></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
    <div class="band-head"><h2 id="faq-title">Questions worth answering upfront</h2></div>

    <h3>What happens if I stop paying?</h3>
    <p>
      The premium rows switch off and you get a message naming exactly which ones. The approval
      gate, your keyword blocklist, the audit trail and tamper detection keep running. BotApprove
      does not leave your server and does not stop screening bots over money.
    </p>

    <h3>Do I lose my settings?</h3>
    <p>
      No. Your whitelist, keywords, approver roles and configuration are kept. Paying again
      restores everything with nothing to reconfigure.
    </p>

    <h3>How do I cancel?</h3>
    <p>
      From your server's dashboard, under Licence, choose Manage billing. If you cannot reach the
      dashboard<% if (portalUrl) { %>, use the
      <a href="<%= portalUrl %>" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">billing portal</a>
      and enter the email you paid with<% } else { %>, contact the operator<% } %>. Cancelling stops
      future charges and premium stays active until the period you already paid for ends.
    </p>

    <h3>Is there a refund?</h3>
    <p>
      No. Payments are non-refundable, including partial months after a cancellation. Cancelling
      stops future charges rather than refunding past ones. If you are a consumer somewhere with a
      statutory right to cancel a digital purchase, that right still applies. See the
      <a href="/terms">Terms</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>How do I activate it?</h3>
    <p>
      Redeem a licence key with <code>/license redeem</code> in your server, or paste it into the
      licence field on your server's dashboard page.
    </p>

    <h3>Is there a separate RaidProtector subscription?</h3>
    <p>
      No, and there will not be. One purchase, one checkout, both bots. Two billing systems is two
      ways for money to go wrong.
    </p>

    <h3>Does buying it twice cover two servers?</h3>
    <p>Yes. A licence covers one server, and both bots in it.</p>

    <h3>Does the free tier expire?</h3>
    <p>
      No. There is no trial countdown on the core gate and no feature that quietly stops working.
      Free means free.
    </p>

    <h3>Why is the nuke bot database paid?</h3>
    <p>
      Because it is the part that takes real maintenance: every submission is reviewed by hand
      before a bot is listed. The invite-and-approve gate is sound protection on its own, so it
      stays free.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="start-title">
    <h2 id="start-title">Start with the free gate</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Add BotApprove first and use it free. Upgrade later if you want the threat list and
      automation.
    </p>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn" href="<%= inviteUrl %>">Add to Discord</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/login">Sign in to the dashboard</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<%- include('partials/foot') %>
